                <pb facs="0875" n="751" sameAs="frus:frus1881/pg751"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2 in No 140.]</seg></opener>
                <head>Telegram. Deposited in Chihuahua, November 24, 1880. Received in the palace
                    the 29th of the same month and the same year at 8.38 a.m.</head>
                <p rendition="#flush">To the <hi rendition="#small-caps">Secretary of Foreign
                        Affairs</hi>:</p>
                <p>The band of marauders, headed by the American bandit Robert E. Martin continues
                    to commit robberies on the inhabitants of Janos and Ascencion, who solicit
                    relief, and as they are exasperated at seeing their property disappear, it is to
                    be feared that upon making the pursuit, as they say they will, they may pass the
                    dividing line, and if they engage the robbers in a fight, it may cause a
                    conflict.</p>
                <closer><signed>TERRAZAS.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
